  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="087c951d-d1e9-5f5a-9524-0130ab716b20" activityNameId="6b3ec77b-ae5c-5a5b-8dd8-0b32cdcb0dcb" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Regional train</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Regional train
The exchanges of the train manufacturing are derived from an assessment of the "Kolibri", a regional train which is currently used for regional transportation in Switzerland .The life span of the train  is assumed to be 40 years resulting in a life time performance of  6’000’000 vkm.  Total weight of the train is about 171t. The dominating material is steel.;
UUID: a2583d65-566d-3488-96fc-285b42476e21
This inventory calls processes of material production, representing the material composition of a standard Swiss Regional Train (Kolibri). For manufacturing, electricity and light oil burned in industrial furnace are included. For the transportation of materials standard distance are applied.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: In 2000 the modelled train dominates the regional transport in Switzerland. However, in the near future new trains will be in operation, which are characterised by a substitution of steel with aluminium.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: The data of the material composition and energy consumption is based on oral communication with an expert of one company and literature studies. 
Extrapolations: This train type is used as an estimate for the entire regional train fleet.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a2583d65-566d-3488-96fc-285b42476e21.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
